A||||8||LPR||Can we make it?||||5||
Z||000000||LPR||03-26-2001||08:00 PM||||OK, here is the situation.  I'm getting married this summer, Aug 4th, and my fiancee and I have planned a road trip up to PEI, about a 10 hour drive (one way), for our honeymoon.  The "situation" is that I would like to take my 84 2m4 up so we could enjoy having the car on the trip (we realize the lack of luggage space  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> )<BR>A little about my car.  New "used" engine, new sensors, new clutch, new "used" computer, and new tires.  The engine temp gage always says cold but the fan comes on, it dosn't work for some reason. Um the idle races sometimes, but never stops.... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>So, we want to know what you think, can we make it?  If we don't then I'm gonna hear about it for the rest of my life!  How has your "similar" car preformed on long trips?<BR>Luc, husband to be  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||LPR||03-26-2001||09:13 PM||||advice please!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000002||85Josh||03-26-2001||09:17 PM||||My 85 4cyl. recently performed perfectly on a 12-hour round trip. I had only had her for about two weeks, and hadn't done anything but change the oil. I have the same temp guage/idle speed problems. Congratulations, and Good Luck!<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4<BR>CAVALRY SCOUT!(stuck in Field Artillery)<p>[This message has been edited by 85Josh (edited 03-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||LarryB||03-26-2001||09:24 PM||||Rent a car.  You're probably going to be driving along some pretty remote stretches (think of I-95 between Bangor and Houlton as an example) and if you do break down along the way there's a good chance finding a suitable part for a Fiero quickly and at a reasonable price will be a challenge.  <P>If you rent a car and something happens, it's on their dime, not yours. ||||reg||3
Z||000004||stimpy||03-27-2001||01:23 PM||||Any other trip, I'd say enjoy the adventure & take the Fiero. On your honeymoon RENT A CAR! You really do not want to risk ANY kind of hassle or delay on your honeymoon. The peace of mind is well worth the $.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ChadMan||03-27-2001||01:37 PM||||I'd say rent a car.  My 84 left me stranded three times - twice with blown fusible links and once with a bad fuel pump.||||reg||13
Z||000006||Cheever2||03-27-2001||02:05 PM||||On the other hand, that's the stuff memories are made of.  My 66 Mustang tires were absolutely bald, so I borrowed my Grandma's 65 Falcon.  The steering wheel was HUGE.  We still laugh about that honeymoon trip, 19 years later.  Nothing broke down, though, so it's easy to laugh.  <P><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000007||LPR||03-27-2001||02:19 PM||||Wow! Thanks for all of the advice!  I asked the question hoping that the Fiero would be backed up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> but the "no’s" seem to have it... Oh well, you get what you ask for... It would really suck to break down!!<BR>I would like to say that this site is so great and I have never seen so many helpful people!  My Fiero and I thank you!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Luc<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000008||noyb||03-27-2001||08:45 PM||||Marriage is a marvelous institution.  But who, in their right minds, would commit themselves to an institution?||||reg||1
